  "details": "It seems to added \"Suggesting Localization\" page on the user doccumentation. However, this page contains somethings incorrect. \n\nFirst, strings are approved by proofreaders who are in the translation community, not VRChat devs.\n\nhttps://docs.vrchat.com/docs/suggesting-localization-changes#adding-a-suggestion:~:text=Anything%20with%20a%20green%20check%20has%20already%20been%20approved%20by%20a%20VRChat%20dev%20and%20likely%20does%20not%20need%20further%20suggestions.\n\nSecond, contributers of localization usually use Discord to disscuss about texts, not on Crowdin disscussion (to avoid things are going to a mess).\n\nhttps://docs.vrchat.com/docs/suggesting-localization-changes#adding-a-suggestion:~:text=Post%20comments%20and%20questions%20here%20that%20devs%20and%20community%20members%20can%20respond%20to.\n\nTheir server is linked in the discription on the Crowdin project, or here:\n\nhttps://discord.gg/U2fzWPkfKc",
